=============================
📌 EP01 – INTRO TO FOR LOOPS IN DART
=============================

🔷 1️⃣ What is a For Loop?

A for loop is used when you want to repeat some code a fixed number of times.

🔹 What is a For Loop?

A for loop repeats a block of code a fixed number of times. 
Useful when you know how many times you want to repeat.


It has 3 parts:

for (initialization; condition; update) {
  // code to repeat
}

✔ Initialization → Runs only once (starting point)
✔ Condition → Loop runs while this is true
✔ Update → Changes the counter in every loop

🔷 2️⃣ Basic Syntax

for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
  print(i);
}

Output:
0
1
2
3
4

🔷 3️⃣ Example 1 (Simple Counter)

for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
  print("Number: $i");
}

Explanation: Prints numbers 1 to 5.

🔷 4️⃣ Example 2 (Print Even Numbers)

for (int i = 2; i <= 10; i += 2) {
  print("Even: $i");
}

Explanation: Loop jumps by +2, so it prints even numbers.

🟩 7️⃣ Why Use For Loop?

✔ When number of iterations is known
✔ Easy, predictable, and fast
✔ Best for indexing lists